Bonus chart: The risks
 
 By Madison Mills 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Data: Company filings; Chart: Erin Davis/Axios Don't say you weren't warned. Anthropic's IPO filing includes a long list of risks. Yes, yes, the catastrophic ones — the end of humanity and so on. 

 Also, perhaps scarier for investors: 

 Anthropic says it has committed hundreds of billions of dollars to cloud computing and equipment leases, even as customers can reduce their usage relatively quickly. Some agreements require minimum payments regardless of demand, and the company warns that failing to meet certain obligations could trigger defaults elsewhere, potentially accelerating debt repayments and jeopardizing access to computing infrastructure. Anthropic also acknowledges that it previously underestimated its compute needs. But overestimating future demand could leave it paying for expensive, underused infrastructure. 
 
 
